  doi = {10.1126/science.1092666},
  urldate = {2024-01-24},
  abstract = {摘要 The impact of global air pollution on climate and the environment is a new focus in atmospheric science. Intercontinental transport and hemispheric air pollution by ozone jeopardize agricultural and natural ecosystems worldwide and have a strong effect on climate. Aerosols, which are spread globally but have a strong regional imbalance, change global climate through their direct and indirect effects on radiative forcing. In the 1990s, nitrogen oxide emissions from Asia surpassed those from North America and Europe and should continue to exceed them for decades. International initiatives to mitigate global air pollution require participation from both developed and developing countries. 全球空气污染对气候和环境的影响是大气科学的一个新焦点。跨洲际运输和半球性的臭氧空气污染威胁着全球的农业和自然生态系统，并对气候产生强烈影响。气溶胶在全球范围内传播，但区域分布不均衡，通过对辐射强迫的直接和间接影响改变了全球气候。在上世纪90年代，亚洲的氮氧化物排放超过了北美和欧洲，并且在未来几十年内预计将继续超过它们。减轻全球空气污染的国际倡议需要发达国家和发展中国家的参与。},
