  title = {Gains and Losses in the Development of Comprehensive Education in {{China}}},
  author = {Vilairat, Suthisatha},
  year = 2019,
  journal = {Fudan Education Forum},
  volume = {17},
  number = {6},
  pages = {12--17},
  issn = {1672-0059},
  urldate = {2023-05-21},
  abstract = {Through 70 years of development, Chinese education has adhered to the education policy of talent cultivation, and remarkable achievements have been made. Nowadays, China is gradually moving towards an educationally powerful country with an international perspective. The above outline is the basic contents and directions of comprehensive education policy which is proper and accurate. From the perspective of Chinese Thai people, this paper analyzes the gains and losses in the development of comprehensive education in China since the implementation of the reform and opening-up policy. It also discusses the countermeasures to the problems existing in the reform and development of education in China with the conclusion that China's comprehensive education needs to consider the overall situation, adapting to the needs of China's global economic and social development. Equal attention must be paid to cultural and scientific knowledge as well as moral cultivation education. China's comprehensive education can eventually cultivate more talents with both excellent moral character and adaptability to the harmonious development of society. It can help China meet the needs of its rapid economic development and a respectable international image.},
