  abstract = {Domestic violence is not uncommon in China. Myths and misconceptions about it do exist, especially in the context of rapid social changes. Compared with its Western counterparts, the study on domestic violence in China is considered rudimentary and of low priority. Empirical studies, especially those measuring the correlates and/or risk factors related to domestic violence, are still lacking. This special issue aims to advance understanding on domestic violence through much-needed empirical research. It also demonstrates joint efforts by local Chinese scholars and their Western counterparts to strengthen collaboration in this important research area. Based on relatively large sample surveys, the articles incorporated in this special issue provide relatively accurate estimates of factors related to domestic violence and responses to it in mainland China and Taiwan. Future studies should give priority to developing indigenous theories and practices in addition to adapting and testing theories and models developed in the West. 家庭暴力在中国并不少见。关于家庭暴力的误解和误区确实存在，尤其是在快速社会变革的背景下。与西方国家相比，中国对家庭暴力的研究被认为是初步的且优先级较低。实证研究，尤其是那些衡量与家庭暴力相关的关联因素和/或风险因素的研究，仍然缺乏。本期特刊旨在通过急需的实证研究来加深对家庭暴力的理解。它还展示了中国本土学者与西方同行在这一重要研究领域加强合作的共同努力。基于相对较大的样本调查，本期特刊中的文章提供了关于中国大陆和台湾地区与家庭暴力相关因素及其应对措施的相对准确的估计。未来的研究应优先发展本土理论和实践，除了适应和测试在西方发展出的理论和模型之外。},
  langid = {english},
  file = {C:\Users\HuYG0\OneDrive\Papers\2018.Zhang.Empirical Research on Domestic Violence in Contemporary China Continuity and Advances.pdf}
}

